MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The resistors and LEDs fit my breadboards, PCB boards and small components because I can use them together in simple circuit experiments.",
    "The magnet wire connects directly to my ferrite toroid cores and gives me a plausible next step for winding small coils, provided the gauge suits the project."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The oscilloscope, signal generator and bench power supply relate to electronics, but I have no current testing task that makes me want those instruments. The banana leads also assume matching equipment that my purchases do not establish.",
    "The linear rail and filament assume a 3D printing project I have not shown, while the strong cup magnets assume a mounting need that my fastener purchases alone do not establish."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My small electronics purchases seem to have been treated as interest in an entire equipped electronics workbench.",
    "My casters and fasteners seem to have been stretched into interest in precision machinery and other mounting hardware without a specific project connecting them."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "A useful connection for me is whether an item works directly with components I have already bought, such as resistors with LEDs or winding wire with ferrite cores.",
    "My purchases span separate tasks over several years, so an older component purchase suggests a possible interest rather than proving that the project is still active. I choose selectively when there is a clear use now."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The suggestions recognized my circuit tinkering but extended it too far into specialized equipment and projects I have not established."
}
